# Keep frontend builds reproducible across Linux CI and Windows releases.
frontend/** text=auto eol=lf
docs/** text=auto eol=lf

# These scripts execute inside a Linux container. A CRLF shebang fails before
# the launcher can log anything, so keep Docker shell launchers explicitly LF.
packaging/docker/*.sh text eol=lf

# The served bundle is a BUILD ARTIFACT that is also tracked (Flask serves
# frontend/dist, and releases ship it). That combination makes it the single
# most dangerous path in an upstream merge: taking upstream's `build(frontend):`
# commit reintroduces the cloud-engine Setup UI this fork removed, and it does
# so with no source change to notice. It has happened, and on 2026-07-27
# upstream's incoming bundle carried all six strings the local-only contract
# test forbids.
#
# `-merge` unsets the merge attribute, so git NEVER content-merges these files:
# any upstream change to them becomes an explicit conflict with this fork's
# version left in the tree. Resolve it the way FORK_NOTES' merge routine says --
# keep ours, then rebuild with `cd frontend && npm run build` in a separate
# build(frontend): commit. Never `git checkout --theirs` here.
frontend/dist/** -merge
